It matters as a substrate health metric - it measures whether the crawling/searching motor pattern is physically stable, separate from whether the creature finds the ball. A policy can have a great contact rate while flinging itself around so violently that it regularly ends up past the tilt limit - that was exactly the +22.5pt curriculum run's profile (best vision gap, worst tip rate), which is what motivated the posture experiment.

One nuance: an episode that ends in a tip is also an episode where the search got cut short, so tip rate and contact rate aren't fully independent - a tip is both "fell over" and "lost its chance to reach the ball."

