4. Shape × displacement interaction. Shape-invariance was only tested at offset 0. Running the shape battery under prism displacement would test whether the color-steering and shape-agnosticism hold up together, and is cheap (eval-only, no retraining).
5. Longer-horizon / richer cue. The "approach red" rule is real but narrow and arguably brittle (a single chromatic channel at 32×32). If you want to push toward richer interpenetration, a higher-resolution camera would let shape compete with color, and is the natural test of whether the color-dominance is a resolution artifact or a genuine learned preference.

